# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository and checked out with LF
# on every platform. The shell scripts must have LF line endings to run under
# bash (a CRLF `set -o pipefail` or shebang is rejected), and the release and
# format versions are single-sourced by a text check (scripts/sync-version.sh),
# so a Windows checkout must be byte-identical to a Linux or macOS one
# (NFR-010; release.md, "Environments & Promotion": a release is built from the
# exact revision that passed continuous integration).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Bundled fonts are binary data and are never normalized (NFR-040).
assets/fonts/*.ttf binary
assets/fonts/*.otf binary
crates/vectr-project/assets/fonts/*.ttf binary
crates/vectr-project/assets/fonts/*.otf binary
